  "description": "SATJUU crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C127 H198 Dy6 Mn6 O54 P6,2.5(C2 H3 N1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 7 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.338-4.035 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.60-119.82°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C127H198Dy6Mn6O54P6·2.5(C2H3N)·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
